DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The current state of a device is accessed by calling ddeevviiccee__ggeett__ssttaattee()
     which returns DS_NOTPRESENT, DS_ALIVE, DS_ATTACHED or DS_BUSY (described
     in device(9)).  To test see if a device was successfully probed, call
     ddeevviiccee__iiss__aalliivvee() which simply returns if the state is greater or equal
     to DS_ALIVE.  To test see if a device was successfully attached, call
     ddeevviiccee__iiss__aattttaacchheedd() which simply returns if the state is greater or
     equal to DS_ATTACHED.

     Each device has a busy count which is incremented when ddeevviiccee__bbuussyy() is
     called and decremented when ddeevviiccee__uunnbbuussyy() is called.  Both routines re‐
     turn an error if the device state is less than DS_ATTACHED.

     When ddeevviiccee__bbuussyy() is called on a device in the DS_ATTACHED state, the
     device changes to the DS_BUSY state.  When ddeevviiccee__uunnbbuussyy() is called and
     after decrementing, the busy count for the device is zero, the device
     changes to the DS_ATTACHED state.

